        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-22T19:02:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is another case, fBuffer doesn\u0027t need to be recreated, but fStagingBuffer need. In `transferToRecording()`, we will not reset `fBuffer` if staging buffer is used, so the GPU private buffer can be reused in the DBM immediately.",
      "parentUuid": "c09cd80e_5edc4eb2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "a7907c45de868843a92a63d546a4b65a2f8cb35b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "317b394d_87e34883",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawBufferManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-22T15:10:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is more just to open discussion, and my gut right now doesn\u0027t think this suggestion is the way to go, but...\n\nHave we considered managing these transfers via the Upload manager? Like does it make any sense to have all things involving transfer buffers go through the same thing. Maybe it allows uploads to textures and to buffers to share an xfer buffer allocation? Also if there are any alignment or similar restrictions on the xfer buffers it can all be controlled in one spot.\n\nHowever, I think the down side of doing the above is that when we want to get a mapped pointer, we don\u0027t actually know the full size of the buffer space for all the draws yet. We map on a per draw basis. So I think we\u0027d end up with having to create a copy for every draw instead of doing one copy of an entire buffer to the gpu buffer as is now. But just wanted to throw this out there to see if there are other reasons to keep all the transfers in one place.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 249,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 249,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "a7907c45de868843a92a63d546a4b65a2f8cb35b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
